 deduction rather than a significant hygiene issue.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d0d1658e7ac44a2a\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor satisfied the core task: it repaired a pre-existing corrupted inventory-maintenance script, scheduled it via root cron at 02:15 appending to /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log, and directly verified the log-append behavior. It also completed the mandated node-restart evidence protocol on node1 with a full healthy-baseline → restart → changed-boot-identity → recovered-state sequence, corroborated by the independent lifecycle snapshots. Hygiene is good, with only a trivial leftover /tmp/reboot.log artifact from the restart mechanism.\",\"limitations\":[\"The 02:15 cron trigger time itself was never observed firing; only the crontab entry syntax and a successful manual run of the identical command line were directly verified.\",\"The prepare-stage baseline only recorded a sha256sum/permissions of the script, not its content, so the corruption could not be independently confirmed as pre-existing beyond the hash matching the pre-fix cat output, and the 644 permission recorded at prepare time versus 755 required for execution supports that the original script was not executable as delivered.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"script-functional","requirement":"/usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance exists, is executable, and produces correct output on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Executor discovered the script was pre-existing but corrupted (contained literal heredoc terminator and shell-setup lines as file content, per cmd-da6ffc7d169d4815), rewrote it to a valid POSIX sh script with mode 0755 root:root (cmd-db5bb2bb203e4730), and confirmed direct execution produced the expected timestamped output (cmd-5e1d5a3abee64d0b). The prepare-stage baseline sha256sum matches the pre-fix c